    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7998eef2_83b477e3",
        "filename": "keymaster/4.1/IKeymasterDevice.hal",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1071728
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-27T20:19:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Android devices typically can be unlocked either using a credential (pin, pattern or password) or a biometric (fingerprint, face, etc) but there are certain scenarios where the credential (Gatekeeper) is the only authenticator that can be used such as first unlock after a device boot, biometric timeout (every 72 hours) and lockdown mode (user can disable the use of biometrics for unlock). While biometrics provide ease of access, credentials provide knowledge-based authentication which is stronger especially for storage encryption.\n\nCan we bind keyguard bound keys (keys bound to UNLOCKED_DEVICE_REQUIRED) to this property and enforce this in keymaster. Keymaster can maintain the state and will allow the appropriate authenticator to unlock keyguard bound keys.\n\nAn input parameter to this API that denotes *Gatekeeper only* would be required to achieve this ?",
      "revId": "8729a9486575e35b62108a832b47fee23c2ea60f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
